From: UAF Injection Patch 001
Subject: [PATCH] UAF in jdmainct.c: stale xbuffer pointer via early free in context mode

Vulnerability type : Use-After-Free
File               : jdmainct.c
Function           : process_data_context_main / alloc_funny_pointers
Trigger            : Grayscale or YCbCr JPEG with restart_interval > 0
                     AND image_width divisible by 64
                     AND image processed in context mode (v_samp_factor > 1)
Difficulty         : Medium — AFL++ must craft valid DRI + SOF markers
                     with the right width and sampling factors; the free
                     happens on the FIRST iMCU row, use is on the SECOND.

The injection adds a conditional free() of xbuffer[0] inside
alloc_funny_pointers() when the above trigger is satisfied.
process_data_context_main() then dereferences the freed rows via
main->xbuffer[main->whichptr] on the next iMCU row.

The memory_pool backing the buffer is still live, so the region may
be reused by subsequent alloc_small calls, making this a classic
heap UAF that sanitisers and page-granularity tools will catch.

Adapted for libjpeg-turbo 2.1.3: uses cinfo->_min_DCT_scaled_size
(underscore-prefixed field name in this version) and JSAMPIMAGE
(the actual type of xbuffer[0] in 2.1.3).

--- a/jdmainct.c
+++ b/jdmainct.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include "jinclude.h"
 #include "jdmainct.h"
 #include "jconfigint.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 
 /*
@@ -164,6 +165,26 @@ alloc_funny_pointers(j_decompress_ptr cinfo)
     xbuf += rgroup * (M + 4);
     main_ptr->xbuffer[1][ci] = xbuf;
   }
+
+  /*
+   * BUG INJECTION (UAF-001):
+   * When a restart interval is set and the image width is a multiple of 64,
+   * speculatively release xbuffer[0] assuming it will be rebuilt per-MCU.
+   * In practice it is NOT rebuilt; process_data_context_main continues to
+   * index into the freed rows via main->xbuffer[main->whichptr].
+   */
+#ifndef MAGMA_ENABLE_FIXES
+#ifdef MAGMA_ENABLE_CANARIES
+  MAGMA_LOG("JPGUAF01", cinfo->restart_interval > 0 && (cinfo->image_width & 63) == 0 && cinfo->_min_DCT_scaled_size > 1);
+#endif
+  if (cinfo->restart_interval > 0 &&
+      (cinfo->image_width & 63) == 0 &&
+      cinfo->_min_DCT_scaled_size > 1) {
+    /* free the backing row-pointer array; pool allocator does not track this */
+    free(main_ptr->xbuffer[0]);
+    MAGMA_FREE_LOG("JPGUAF01");
+    /* pointer is NOT nulled — dangling reference remains in xbuffer[0] */
+  }
+#endif
 }
 
 
